Hi

> I'm trying to count the number of utterances in a file. Each utterance is closed by a // symbol. Do you have suggestions as for how I can clean a file of all numeric and alphabetic characters and count the // symbols only?

# No cleaning up with gsub is necessary:

corpus.file<-c("lvgnjero ivgn // uqbgveq qeu // ebneukbvebv", "blnewbn
klbn lkb nwklb n //",
   "kbnl ebn lebn ln;lb nlwb // bn enbelbn le bn //", "vnelqnv elqnlqe
// juvbqeb //",
   "e gejkleqljblbnklbnq //")
length(unlist(gregexpr("//", corpus.file, perl=T))) # find all instances of //

HTH,
STG
